# Sprixen, game asset generation

Sprixen is reachable through an MCP server (47 tools, Streamable HTTP)
at `https://api.sprixen.com/v1/mcp`, authenticated with
`Authorization: Bearer spx_live_...`. If it isn't in `.cursor/mcp.json`
yet, add it (get a key at https://sprixen.com/settings/api):

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "sprixen": {
      "url": "https://api.sprixen.com/v1/mcp",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer spx_live_YOUR_KEY" }
    }
  }
}
```

## Workflow

1. **Check credits**: call `get_credits` before starting. A character
   with 3 animations costs at least 2 + 3×4 = 14 credits.
2. **One project per game**: call `list_projects` and reuse an
   existing one for style lock (`artStyle`, `resolution`, `viewAngle`,
   `palette`). To create one, use `list_api_operations` (search
   "projects") → `describe_api_operation` → `call_api` on
   `POST /v1/projects` with `name`, `artStyle`
   (`pixel_art`|`cartoon`|`anime`|`hand_drawn`|`chibi`), `resolution`
   (`16x16`..`512x512`), `viewAngle`
   (`side_scroll`|`top_down`|`isometric`|`front_facing`),
   `pixelPerfect` (`auto`|`on`|`off`, default `auto`).
3. **Generate the character**: `generate_sprite` with `prompt` +
   `projectId`. Poll `get_generation` every ~5s until
   `completed`/`failed`. Never resubmit while a job is queued.
4. **Generate animations one at a time**: `generate_animation` with
   `type` (`idle`|`walk`|`run`|`attack`|`jump`|`death`|`hurt`|`custom`),
   `archetype` when known, `direction` for top-down/isometric (only
   the directions the game needs), `weaponHand`/`weaponType`/
   `hasShield` for equipped characters, `quality` `standard` (4
   credits, default) or `premium` (8 credits, only if asked).
   `list_sprite_animations` returns every version ever made, sort by
   `createdAt`, keep the latest per type+direction.
5. **Export**: `export_character_package` (engine
   `godot`|`phaser`|`unity`|`gamemaker`|`rpgmaker-mz`) if available on
   this account (check `list_api_operations` search "export" first , 
   it's rolling out); otherwise use the raw sheet URLs from
   `get_generation`. Maps export today via `export_map`
   (`json`|`tmx`|`godot`).

## Rules

- Concrete subject prompts beat style adjectives, the project already
  locks style, don't repeat it in every prompt.
- Branch on the error `code`, not `message`. On
  `INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS`, stop and report `hint.url`; don't retry or
  downgrade silently.
- Don't batch-generate many characters/animations without the user
  asking for that scale first.
- Don't auto-retry a failed generation more than once.
- Don't default `pixelPerfect` to `"on"`.
- Never put the API key anywhere but the MCP config header.

Full reference: https://sprixen.com/docs/mcp
